<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alba Iulia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gyulafehérvár, Karlsburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alba Iulia, in Hungarian Gyulafehérvár, is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, on the Mureș River, built on the site of the Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> fortress of Apulum. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Transylvania from the 11th century and the capital of the Principality of Transylvania in the 16th and 17th centuries. On 1 December 1918 an assembly there proclaimed the union of Transylvania with Romania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alba-iulia.jpg" alt="Alba Iulia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mihai Raducanu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cetatea_Alba_Carolina_Ansamblul_fortifica%C8%9Biei_%E2%80%9ECetatea_Alba_Iulia_14.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
